WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:11.746
Are you ready to learn? Grab your Bible comfortably. Do you love your Bible? You need it.

2
00:00:11.746 --> 00:00:24.306
Lord, we need You. We need Your Spirit to change us and to move our hearts

3
00:00:24.306 --> 00:00:33.306
for what moves Your heart. And to do Your will. And I pray that it will be done. Amen.

4
00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:50.306
I want to teach this morning about the house of prayer. And about how the Lord is restoring houses of prayer across all nations.

5
00:00:50.306 --> 00:01:00.306
And I want to speak very specifically about the priority of corporate prayer.

6
00:01:00.306 --> 00:01:14.306
Jesus said, my Father's house shall be a house of prayer for people from all nations.

7
00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:21.306
This is the definition. This is the design.

8
00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:30.306
This is what the Lord was looking for when He walked into the temple in the flesh.

9
00:01:30.306 --> 00:01:43.306
If you look at the history of Israel, they were never given the command, just go do something.

10
00:01:43.306 --> 00:01:50.306
They were given very specific instructions.

11
00:01:50.306 --> 00:01:56.306
The house of the Lord comes from somewhere.

12
00:01:56.306 --> 00:02:04.306
The design came from the design of heaven.

13
00:02:04.306 --> 00:02:16.306
So if you look in Exodus, when Moses is told how he received the instructions for the tabernacle,

14
00:02:16.306 --> 00:02:31.306
he did not just set up something he thought would work.

15
00:02:31.306 --> 00:02:34.306
He had to meet God.

16
00:02:34.306 --> 00:02:39.306
He had to meet God face to face.

17
00:02:49.306 --> 00:02:56.306
He was commanded, go and follow the pattern as you received it on the mountain.

18
00:02:56.306 --> 00:02:58.306
There is a pattern.

19
00:02:59.306 --> 00:03:01.306
There is a blueprint.

20
00:03:03.306 --> 00:03:06.306
We do not just do what we want here.

21
00:03:14.306 --> 00:03:21.306
May I suggest that just because time has passed, God has not changed His mind?

22
00:03:29.306 --> 00:03:31.306
It is still the way of God.

23
00:03:39.306 --> 00:03:43.306
So I want to talk to you about the priority of Corporate Prayer.

24
00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:47.306
I want to provide the secret place.

25
00:03:47.306 --> 00:03:54.306
We know that we must build a life with God in the secret place, for that is what He seeks.

26
00:03:58.306 --> 00:04:06.306
And then I assume that you have a personal prayer life, for we know how important it is to meet God Himself in that secret place.

27
00:04:16.306 --> 00:04:24.306
But when we seek God together, something happens. Then we understand the will of God for us as a whole.

28
00:04:29.306 --> 00:04:34.306
Not this morning, but the next, the first week of September.

29
00:04:34.306 --> 00:04:41.306
And I want to urge us to make commitments to the Corporate House called Prayer.

30
00:04:41.306 --> 00:04:47.306
And starting in September, so not tomorrow, but starting in September we will resume on Mondays and Thursdays.

31
00:04:47.306 --> 00:04:55.306
And I really want to urge you to dedicate yourself to this and to come.

32
00:04:59.306 --> 00:05:02.306
Let’s turn together to Acts 15.

33
00:05:03.306 --> 00:05:08.306
And this may be a bit unfamiliar, but that’s okay.

34
00:05:08.306 --> 00:05:12.306
And maybe you don’t know this passage very well, and that’s fine.

35
00:05:27.306 --> 00:05:31.306
Acts 15 takes place in the early days of the early church.

36
00:05:31.306 --> 00:05:37.306
Jesus has risen, He has ascended to heaven, and the apostles are proclaiming the gospel.

37
00:05:46.306 --> 00:05:52.306
And the context of Acts 15 is that there is a huge influx of Gentiles being saved.

38
00:06:02.306 --> 00:06:09.306
So you have a whole Jewish church, Jesus was a Jew and He is the Messiah.

39
00:06:15.306 --> 00:06:20.306
And the root into which we are grafted is the Jewish faith.

40
00:06:22.306 --> 00:06:24.306
There is history in the story.

41
00:06:25.306 --> 00:06:27.306
There is more than just us.

42
00:06:32.306 --> 00:06:37.306
So we are vaccinated into a story that goes all the way back to Abraham.

43
00:06:48.306 --> 00:06:56.306
So here at the beginning of Acts 15, there must really be a significant change in thinking, in Jewish thinking.

44
00:07:02.306 --> 00:07:09.306
And I would say that we are now in a season where the Gentile church needs to make such a mindset shift.

45
00:07:15.306 --> 00:07:23.306
We are 2000 years later, the gospel has gone through all nations, and now it is important that the Gentiles understand where they come from.

46
00:07:32.306 --> 00:07:37.306
That we do not think that we stand alone in the story and that we are just making something up as we go along.

47
00:07:42.306 --> 00:07:46.306
We are part of that history and the story of God is eternal.

48
00:07:47.306 --> 00:07:59.306
If you have the desire to know God and not just to know what is going on in your heart but also how God thinks, then there lies eternity there.

49
00:08:10.306 --> 00:08:12.306
The story is the story of God.

50
00:08:12.306 --> 00:08:17.306
So as we step into that, it is important that we know who He is and what He does.

51
00:08:43.306 --> 00:08:50.306
And what happens here in Acts 15 is that the Gentiles are coming in and the Jews are talking to each other.

52
00:08:50.306 --> 00:08:58.306
And they have the mindset that they must come back under the law of Moses, they must be circumcised to be true followers.

53
00:08:58.306 --> 00:09:07.306
And Paul and Barnabas hear this and go to Jerusalem, and then there is the council of Jerusalem where they discuss together.

54
00:09:29.306 --> 00:09:35.306
You know Paul, he was a Jew from the tribe of Benjamin, he was the Pharisee of Pharisees.

55
00:09:35.306 --> 00:09:44.306
His testimony is that he has met Jesus, that he has seen the risen Lord and that he is sent to the Gentiles to preach Jesus.

56
00:09:48.306 --> 00:09:52.306
And so he was sent to those Gentiles to preach there.

57
00:09:59.306 --> 00:10:03.306
And he sees that the nations come to faith.

58
00:10:08.306 --> 00:10:12.306
He sees that they believe through faith in Jesus.

59
00:10:12.306 --> 00:10:28.306
That they believe the good news of the gospel, that Jesus has come, that he has died, that he has risen, that he has gone to heaven and that he will come back again.

60
00:10:35.306 --> 00:10:40.306
And he sees that they accept that by faith and that the Holy Spirit fills them.

61
00:10:43.306 --> 00:10:50.306
So he comes before that council and he gives his testimony.

62
00:10:50.306 --> 00:10:57.306
And Peter is there and Peter testifies. We see a change among the nations, it's incredible.

63
00:10:57.306 --> 00:11:04.306
The Jews thought that God is for us and with us, and God said no, not only, I am also for the rest.

64
00:11:04.306 --> 00:11:06.306
And they come in.

65
00:11:06.306 --> 00:11:18.306
And Peter is there and they explain, listen, we see that the Gentiles are coming to faith and where the Jews thought it was for us and for us alone, they show, no.

66
00:11:28.306 --> 00:11:33.306
And in verse 13, James then takes the floor and he says

67
00:11:37.306 --> 00:11:39.306
He says brothers, listen.

68
00:11:48.306 --> 00:11:55.306
Simeon or Peter has laid out how God Himself has conceived the plan to form a people from the Gentiles that honors His name.

69
00:12:06.306 --> 00:12:21.306
This corresponds with the words of the prophets. In other words, this is correct. The whole Scripture, the prophets have already spoken about this.

70
00:12:21.306 --> 00:12:26.306
And then James says, as it is written, verse 16,

71
00:12:30.306 --> 00:12:32.306
And James then says, as it is written,

72
00:12:35.306 --> 00:12:38.306
And then he quotes, then I will return to my steps.

73
00:12:42.306 --> 00:12:45.306
I will rebuild the fallen house of David.

74
00:12:48.306 --> 00:12:50.306
From the ruins I will rebuild it again.

75
00:12:52.306 --> 00:12:54.306
And I will cause this house to rise again.

76
00:13:04.306 --> 00:13:09.306
So that, in other words, there is a consequence that will take place.

77
00:13:15.306 --> 00:13:19.306
So that the remnant of the people will seek the Lord.

78
00:13:22.306 --> 00:13:25.306
As well as the Gentiles over whom my name has been called.

79
00:13:29.306 --> 00:13:32.306
So speaks the Lord who has announced this from of old.

80
00:13:41.306 --> 00:13:46.306
James uses Amos 9 to confirm what they see happening.

81
00:13:52.306 --> 00:13:58.306
And that corresponds greatly with the passage from Isaiah 65, 56.

82
00:14:10.306 --> 00:14:16.306
In Isaiah 56, that is the part that Jesus quotes when he enters the temple and says,

83
00:14:16.306 --> 00:14:19.306
my Father's house shall be a house of prayer for all nations.

84
00:14:22.306 --> 00:14:28.306
And salvation will go out to the Gentiles.

85
00:14:39.306 --> 00:14:45.306
And in Isaiah 56 God says, I will receive their offering in my house of prayer.

86
00:14:52.306 --> 00:14:58.306
And do not be surprised if you see that happening, for I will accept their worship,

87
00:14:58.306 --> 00:15:02.306
I will receive their worship in my house that is called prayer.

88
00:15:05.306 --> 00:15:07.306
And this is what we are waiting for.

89
00:15:12.306 --> 00:15:14.306
And that is what God is waiting for.

90
00:15:15.306 --> 00:15:22.306
And that is what God is waiting for. God says, I am waiting for the moment that this is something from all over the world.

91
00:15:28.306 --> 00:15:34.306
Where worship will be present in every nation, tribe, and language.

92
00:15:44.306 --> 00:15:49.306
And salvation goes to the Gentiles. God said that something else would happen.

93
00:15:59.306 --> 00:16:05.306
God says, I will restore that fallen house of David.

94
00:16:05.306 --> 00:16:09.306
God says, I will restore that fallen house of David.

95
00:16:14.306 --> 00:16:19.306
I will ensure that those ruins rise again.

96
00:16:23.306 --> 00:16:28.306
So that in every nation, they will worship me.

97
00:16:29.306 --> 00:16:30.306
They will seek me.

98
00:16:35.306 --> 00:16:45.306
So that in every nation, tribe, and language houses will arise where people will seek me together and make my name great.

99
00:16:45.306 --> 00:16:55.306
So that in every nation, tribe, and language houses will arise where people will seek me together and make my name great.

100
00:17:16.306 --> 00:17:26.306
And why does James then quote Amos 9 here, where it speaks of in that season God will rebuild the tent of David.

101
00:17:29.306 --> 00:17:31.306
What is the tent of David?

102
00:17:32.306 --> 00:17:34.306
That is the question you may ask here.

103
00:17:46.306 --> 00:17:52.306
What did David do? What made God say, you are a man after my heart.

104
00:18:07.306 --> 00:18:14.306
What David has done is that he restored the house of prayer in Jerusalem.

105
00:18:14.306 --> 00:18:19.306
He appointed worshippers who praised the Lord day and night.

106
00:18:21.306 --> 00:18:22.306
David was a prophet.

107
00:18:24.306 --> 00:18:25.306
He was a prophet king.

108
00:18:26.306 --> 00:18:29.306
I became so excited, because Carolien chose a set.

109
00:18:29.306 --> 00:18:31.306
We are not talking, I do not tell her what I am going to talk about.

110
00:18:31.306 --> 00:18:34.306
But we sang this morning about the root of David.

111
00:18:34.306 --> 00:18:39.306
This is it, Jesus comes from the root of David.

112
00:18:50.306 --> 00:18:53.306
We are in a continuation story.

113
00:18:56.306 --> 00:19:00.306
Why does James say part of the prophet?

114
00:19:00.306 --> 00:19:04.306
Because it is the order of the tabernacle.

115
00:19:04.306 --> 00:19:06.306
The house of prayer.

116
00:19:06.306 --> 00:19:13.306
The house of prayer that will be restored in every landing for the return of the Lord.

117
00:19:22.306 --> 00:19:23.306
Why does he tell that?

118
00:19:25.306 --> 00:19:30.306
So that the rest, the remnant of humanity,

119
00:19:30.306 --> 00:19:32.306
all those people who will believe,

120
00:19:32.306 --> 00:19:34.306
come to seek the Lord in my house.

121
00:19:42.306 --> 00:19:44.306
If we know David's story,

122
00:19:45.306 --> 00:19:49.306
the first thing he does when he becomes king,

123
00:19:50.306 --> 00:19:53.306
the first thing that comes to his mind,

124
00:20:03.306 --> 00:20:08.306
he is anointed and appointed and he still has to wait a long time under Saul.

125
00:20:20.306 --> 00:20:24.306
What you do with your life, what you think about, what you are busy with,

126
00:20:24.306 --> 00:20:26.306
says a whole lot about you.

127
00:20:33.306 --> 00:20:36.306
And with David, we know that the first thing he does,

128
00:20:37.306 --> 00:20:41.306
what David does is that he brings the ark of the covenant of God,

129
00:20:41.306 --> 00:20:44.306
which was parked in a corner somewhere under Saul,

130
00:20:46.306 --> 00:20:47.306
which was ignored.

131
00:20:49.306 --> 00:20:51.306
The ark is the presence.

132
00:20:55.306 --> 00:20:56.306
David,

133
00:20:57.306 --> 00:20:59.306
when you are in your life,

134
00:20:59.306 --> 00:21:01.306
when you are the king of Israel,

135
00:21:01.306 --> 00:21:04.306
I will bring the ark of the covenant back to Jerusalem.

136
00:21:10.306 --> 00:21:14.306
The kingship of Saul was a time of pleasing people.

137
00:21:18.306 --> 00:21:22.306
The kingship of Saul was a time of pleasing people.

138
00:21:25.306 --> 00:21:28.306
The kingship of Saul was a time of pleasing people.

139
00:21:30.306 --> 00:21:36.306
The kingship of Saul was a time when it was about pleasing people.

140
00:21:39.306 --> 00:21:41.306
God did not choose Saul.

141
00:21:42.306 --> 00:21:43.306
Not really.

142
00:21:48.306 --> 00:21:53.306
When you read the story, you read that God did not want Israel to have a man as king.

143
00:22:00.306 --> 00:22:04.306
We just want a man as king. Give us a man and we will be heavy.

144
00:22:15.306 --> 00:22:19.306
So Saul was not God's ultimate choice for Israel.

145
00:22:24.306 --> 00:22:28.306
But what God does, and what He still does,

146
00:22:30.306 --> 00:22:34.306
is if you persist in something,

147
00:22:42.306 --> 00:22:47.306
if you keep pressing your desires before God,

148
00:22:47.306 --> 00:22:50.306
then God will ultimately give you over to those desires.

149
00:22:53.306 --> 00:22:57.306
Be careful with what you push for.

150
00:22:59.306 --> 00:23:02.306
I pushed for it, and I got it, and God blessed it.

151
00:23:02.306 --> 00:23:04.306
And God said, I am not behind that.

152
00:23:13.306 --> 00:23:16.306
Well, I just pushed that door down until it went.

153
00:23:16.306 --> 00:23:18.306
And God did not bless it, did not choose it.

154
00:23:18.306 --> 00:23:23.306
He just waits out that season until you repent and come back.

155
00:23:30.306 --> 00:23:34.306
And maybe it will cost you your whole life.

156
00:23:38.306 --> 00:23:43.306
I worry that many Christians waste their lives in Christ.

157
00:23:48.306 --> 00:23:50.306
Because they go their own way.

158
00:23:51.306 --> 00:23:53.306
And they call it blessed.

159
00:23:55.306 --> 00:23:58.306
And they are frustrated with God.

160
00:23:59.306 --> 00:24:01.306
They do not enjoy worshiping Him.

161
00:24:02.306 --> 00:24:04.306
They don't really love His Word.

162
00:24:05.306 --> 00:24:07.306
They do their thing.

163
00:24:09.306 --> 00:24:11.306
And that hits hard.

164
00:24:12.306 --> 00:24:14.306
But God will wait.

165
00:24:16.306 --> 00:24:20.306
He waits until you repent and return.

166
00:24:23.306 --> 00:24:26.306
And God waits at the point where you took a detour.

167
00:24:28.306 --> 00:24:33.306
And the whole season of Saul is a time when Saul did not seek God.

168
00:24:38.306 --> 00:24:40.306
He did not even restore the future.

169
00:24:40.306 --> 00:24:42.306
The manifest glory was not future in Israel.

170
00:24:42.306 --> 00:24:43.306
I mean, what a leader.

171
00:24:43.306 --> 00:24:47.306
I want to follow no one who does not know the manifest glory of Jesus.

172
00:24:47.306 --> 00:24:49.306
I want no one.

173
00:24:49.306 --> 00:24:50.306
Leader.

174
00:24:50.306 --> 00:24:51.306
Teacher.

175
00:24:51.306 --> 00:24:54.306
Who does not know the glory of God.

176
00:24:59.306 --> 00:25:04.306
Who had the manifest presence of God parked somewhere in a corner.

177
00:25:04.306 --> 00:25:10.306
I do not want to serve a leader who does not know that intense presence of God himself.

178
00:25:13.306 --> 00:25:16.306
For they will not lead you to the right place.

179
00:25:16.306 --> 00:25:22.306
So the whole season of Saul was a season in which he pleased the people.

180
00:25:28.306 --> 00:25:35.306
And God says, I now set David in, who has my heart.

181
00:25:35.306 --> 00:25:41.306
I set him as king of Israel, so that he can lead the people for me.

182
00:25:47.306 --> 00:25:50.306
It is not that David was perfect.

183
00:25:50.306 --> 00:25:52.306
It is not that David never did wrong.

184
00:25:52.306 --> 00:25:53.306
It is none of that.

185
00:25:53.306 --> 00:25:57.306
A human leader will never be the things you are looking for.

186
00:25:57.306 --> 00:26:00.306
And it is not that David was perfect and made no mistakes.

187
00:26:00.306 --> 00:26:06.306
For there is no human leader who can have that perfection.

188
00:26:06.306 --> 00:26:08.306
So do not look to human leaders.

189
00:26:08.306 --> 00:26:18.306
Whether that is in the government or in the church, it does not matter.

190
00:26:18.306 --> 00:26:23.306
That person is only there to point you to God.

191
00:26:24.306 --> 00:26:25.306
And to the Word.

192
00:26:26.306 --> 00:26:27.306
And to the spirit.

193
00:26:28.306 --> 00:26:29.306
And to prayer.

194
00:26:30.306 --> 00:26:31.306
And to prayer.

195
00:26:34.306 --> 00:26:37.306
For how can you know God, who is spirit?

196
00:26:38.306 --> 00:26:43.306
And when David brings the ark back to Jerusalem, it is the first thing he does.

197
00:26:43.306 --> 00:26:45.306
And he says, I want it there.

198
00:26:45.306 --> 00:26:48.306
And then he does something revolutionary.

199
